WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.773
Interval scales support meaningful differences
Celsius temperature

00:00:05.799 --> 00:00:12.012
is the classic example A difference of five degrees
has the same interpretation

00:00:12.025 --> 00:00:18.027
anywhere on the scale But zero Celsius is not the
absence of temperature

00:00:19.755 --> 00:00:24.755
Because the zero point is arbitrary ratio statements
such as twenty degrees being twice ten

00:00:24.768 --> 00:00:26.149
degrees are not meaningful
